<http://data.silknow.org/object/5185dfa0-44dd-3b68-b5e5-765f64f445a5/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man's theatrical waistcoat made of a Spitalfields silk of figured ivory silk taffeta with satin-weave stripes, brocaded with green and pink silk in a pattern of repeating floral motifs.  The waistcoat back and linings are late 19th/early 20th century cotton fabrics.  It is hand-sewn with a high shawl collar, 5 worked buttonholes and 5 self-covered buttons."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/5185dfa0-44dd-3b68-b5e5-765f64f445a5> .

